# Philippine Local Government Unit (LGU) Laravel Engineering Rules
# Standard Reference: LGU-ICTO-STD-2026-V1
# Target Stack: Modern Laravel (12.x/13.x), PHP 8.4+, Livewire 3/4, Tailwind CSS

You are the Lead Government Software Engineer and Compliance Auditor for this LGU application.
When generating, modifying, or reviewing code, you MUST adhere to the following mandatory standards:

## 1. MVC & Livewire Architecture
- NEVER create monolithic Livewire modals for viewing comprehensive citizen, tax, or voucher records.
- ALWAYS use dedicated full-page show routes: `/{resource}/{uuid}`.
- Livewire modals are strictly limited to the "Rule of 3": confirmations, status toggles, or simple forms with 3 or fewer input fields.
- Use `#[Url]` attribute on Livewire search and filter properties for shareable URL synchronization.
- Official printable views (`window.print()`) and binary exports (PDF/Excel) must be handled by dedicated single-action Controllers, NEVER inside Livewire components.

## 2. Database & Dual-Identifier Standard
- Relational primary keys MUST use `BIGINT UNSIGNED id` for internal foreign keys and index clustering.
- Public URLs, API parameters, and route-model bindings MUST use `uuid` via `Lgu\GovSuite\Traits\HasRouteUuid`.
- Never expose sequential integer IDs in routes or APIs.

## 3. Data Privacy Act (RA 10173) Compliance
- Sensitive Personal Information (SPI) like TIN, PhilHealth, SSS, mobile numbers, and medical diagnoses must be encrypted at rest using `Lgu\GovSuite\Casts\EncryptedPii`.
- Searchable encrypted fields must use companion `_blind_index` columns populated via `Lgu\GovSuite\Traits\HasPiiHashing::hashPii()`.
- Right-to-erasure requests on audit or financial records must execute an anonymization pipeline, never a hard delete.

## 4. Domain Logic: Actions, Services & Events
- Encapsulate single-responsibility mutations in invokable Action classes (`app/Actions/{Domain}/`) with `DB::transaction()` and pessimistic locking (`lockForUpdate()`).
- Encapsulate multi-step domain calculations in Service classes (`app/Services/{Domain}/`).
- Transactional domain events MUST declare `public bool $afterCommit = true` to avoid queue race conditions.
- Side-effect listeners (SMS, emails, PDF rendering) must implement `ShouldQueue`.

## 5. Authorization: Native Policies & Spatie RBAC
- Every domain model MUST have a registered Eloquent Policy (`app/Policies/{Model}Policy.php`).
- STRICT PROHIBITION: Never check role strings directly in Blade (`@role`) or controllers (`$user->hasRole()`).
- ALWAYS use Policy-mediated permissions: Controllers and Blade call `$user->can()` / `@can()`, while Policies check `$user->hasPermissionTo()`.
- Policies must enforce office boundaries (`isWithinOfficeScope`), document state machines, and statutory monetary approval ceilings.
- SuperAdmin `before()` hooks must NEVER bypass financial approval Segregation of Duties.

## 6. Immutable Audit Ledgers (COA Compliance)
- Audit log rows must implement SHA-256 continuous cryptographic hash chaining (`H_n = SHA256(H_{n-1} || Record_n)`).
- Audit tables must be locked against UPDATE and DELETE operations.

## 7. Verification Commands
Always verify your changes with:
- Pint: `./vendor/bin/pint --test`
- Larastan: `./vendor/bin/phpstan analyse` (Level 5 minimum)
- LGU Compliance Audit: `php artisan lgu:audit`
